{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Quality Assurance "}, {"type": "position", "content": 11}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 3}, {"type": "level", "content": "A1.2"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use when talking about Quality Assurance."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Understand key information about the concepts, principles, and methodologies in simple spoken and written situations.  Talk about programming techniques, use cases, kinds, and sequences in simple spoken and written situations."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Communicates effectively in English about the communicative topics for this level through the use of appropriate basic vocabulary and grammatical structures.  Identifies general aspects related to Software Programming in short written or spoken conversations about past experiences."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe7n2le03ob11re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Simple Present and Simple Past Tense (review)"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "We use the <strong>simple present</strong> when talking about actions in the present or facts. On the other hand, we use the <strong>simple past</strong> when talking about complete actions in the past. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "<p>We use the <strong>simple present </strong>tense to refer to an action that is repeated or usual. This action can be a habit, a hobby, or a daily event. We can also use this tense to talk about something we often forget or normally don't do.<br /> <br /> Examples:&nbsp;<br /> <i>I</i><i>&nbsp;</i><strong><i>read</i></strong><i>&nbsp;</i><i>about video game programming every day.</i><i>&nbsp;</i><i><br /> He&nbsp;<strong>does not write</strong>&nbsp;practical code.&nbsp;<br /> <strong>Do</strong>&nbsp;you<strong>&nbsp;</strong><strong>know</strong>&nbsp;anything about software debugging?&nbsp;</i><br /> <br /> In addition, we also use the <strong>present simple</strong> to talk about facts or generalizations.</p> <p>Example: <i>&nbsp;Computers&nbsp;</i><strong>perform</strong>&nbsp;automatic tasks all the time.&nbsp;<i><br /> </i><br /> In contrast, we use the <strong>simple past</strong> to refer to an action that started and finished at a specific time in the past, even if the specific time is not mentioned. This tense is also used to talk about habits in the past.&nbsp;<br /> <br /> Examples:&nbsp;<br /> <i>We</i><i>&nbsp;</i><strong><i>studied</i></strong><i>&nbsp;</i><i>Java last semester.</i><i>&nbsp;</i><i><br /> They&nbsp;<strong>didn't include</strong><strong>&nbsp;</strong>all the software features.&nbsp;<br /> <strong>Did</strong> she correct the subroutine errors?</i>&nbsp;<br /> <br /> Additionally, we can also use the <strong>past simple</strong> to talk about past facts or generalizations that are no longer true.</p> <p>Example: <i>Modems&nbsp; <strong>connected</strong>&nbsp;to the internet using copper landlines. </i>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "I always take notes during lectures. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "I usually don't miss any of them. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "What else do you remember? "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Mr. Saenz, the CEO, talked about Software Quality Assurance, or SQA. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "I didn't come to the lecture yesterday. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "What did they talk about?"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Adverbs of frequency (review)"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "We use <strong>adverbs of frequency</strong> to describe how often or frequently we do an activity."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<p><strong>Adverbs of frequency</strong> are placed before the main verb (except with the verb <strong>to be</strong>):</p> <p style=\"text-align: center;\">&nbsp;Subject + adverb of frequency + principal verb + complement</p> <p>Example: <i>They <strong>usually</strong> correct errors before running the program.</i></p> <p>When we the verb <strong>to be </strong>is the main verb of a sentence, the position of the <strong>adverb of frequency </strong>changes:</p> <p style=\"text-align: center;\">Subject + verb to be + adverb of frequency + complement</p> <p>Example: <i>She is <strong>never</strong> satisfied with the final version of the code.</i></p> <p>Take a look at the chart of <strong>adverbs of frequency</strong>:</p>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "However, a more extensive and systematic testing is always performed when a preliminary version of the program is finished. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Certain amount of testing and debugging is usually performed while the code is being written. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "These methods sometimes adopt verified software construction models. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "In my department, we occasionally hear about SQA, but we are never sure of what it is."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":1,\"columns\":1,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<center>Adverbs of Frequency \\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":11,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<center>100%\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<center>Always\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<center>90%\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<center>Usually\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<center>80%\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<center>Generally\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<center>70%\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<center>Often\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<center>50%\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<center>Sometimes\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<center>30%\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<center>Occasionally\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<center>10%\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<center>Hardly ever\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<center>5%\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<center>Rarely\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<center>0%\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<center>Never\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border\"}"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "CEO"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "chief executive officer, manager"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(abbreviation)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Mr. Saenz, the CEO, talked about Software Quality Assurance, or SQA."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n2le03ob11aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to get a clear picture of "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to understand a topic clearly"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Did you get a clear picture of what SQA is?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n2le03ob11aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "monitor "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to control or supervise "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: SQA is the process that monitors software creation in order to avoid errors or bugs in the final product."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n2le03ob11aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "bug "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "error or mistake, especially in software "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I thought SQA wasn't that important, but now I see its relevance in bug detection."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n2le03ob11aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "preliminary"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "before the final part or version, preparatory"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: However, a more extensive and systematic testing is always performed when a preliminary version of the program is finished."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n2le03ob11aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Investigate about SQA according to ISO 9001 in Colombia "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write your findings in your notebooks "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Make a presentation about the key features of SQA according to ISO 9001 "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Share the presentation in class to your teacher and classmates"}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I investigate about SQA and other quality standards "}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write about quality standards "}, {"type": "text", "content": "I make a presentation about quality standards "}, {"type": "text", "content": "I talk about quality standards"}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"_data": [], "type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "id": 0, "template_override": 1}, {"_data": [], "title": "", "type": "audio", "template_override": 1, "id": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"audiosrc": "enpe7n2le03ob11re2aud01", "images": [{"time": "0", "image": "enpe7n2le03ob11re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "text": "<strong>Javier</strong>: Hi, Pablo. I didn't come to the lecture yesterday. I usually don't miss any of them. What did they talk about? </br>\n<strong>Pablo</strong>: Mr. Saenz, the CEO, talked about Software Quality Assurance, or SQA. </br>\n<strong>Javier</strong>: In my department, we occasionally hear about SQA, but we are never sure of what it is. Did you get a clear picture of what SQA is? </br>"}, {"time": "24500", "image": "enpe7n2le03ob11re2img02.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "<strong>Pablo</strong>: Well, I always take notes during lectures. Sure, I can tell you. SQA is the process that monitors software creation in order to avoid errors or bugs in the final product. SQA usually covers all the parts of the software production development. The supervision methods used in SQA correspond to international quality standards. On the other hand, these methods sometimes adopt verified software construction models. </br>\n<strong>Javier</strong>: That is very interesting. I thought SQA wasn't that important, but now I see its relevance in bug detection. What else do you remember? </br>"}, {"time": "66500", "image": "enpe7n2le03ob11re2img03.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "<strong>Pablo</strong>: Certain amount of testing and debugging is usually performed while the code is being written. However, a more extensive and systematic testing is always performed when a preliminary version of the program is finished. The priority of testing varies depending on many factors. For instance, the complexity of the software, competitors taking advantage of problems with the program, the costs of new testing tools, etc. </br>\n<strong>Javier</strong>: It sounds like a complex process, with many steps and factors to consider. </br>\n<strong>Pablo</strong>: It is a complex process. For that reason, one of the ultimate goals of SQA experts is developing artificially intelligent automatic testing software, with the ability to analyze an application from its development stage and carry out systematic tests until its final version. </br>\n<strong>Javier</strong>: Thanks Pablo, your summary was very useful."}], "coverimg": "enpe7n2le03ob11re2img01.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}]}, {"_data": [], "title": "", "type": "video", "template_override": 1, "id": 2, "contents": [{"value": {"video_src": "enpe7n2le03ob11re5vqz01pt1", "images": [{"time": "0", "image": "", "id": 0, "text": ""}]}, "type": "video"}]}, {"_data": [], "title": "", "type": "video", "template_override": 1, "id": 3, "contents": [{"value": {"video_src": "enpe7n2le03ob11re5vqz01pt2", "images": [{"time": "0", "image": "", "id": 0, "text": ""}]}, "type": "video"}]}, {"_data": [], "title": "", "type": "video", "template_override": 1, "id": 4, "contents": [{"value": {"video_src": "enpe7n2le03ob11re5vqz01pt3", "images": [{"time": "0", "image": "", "id": 0, "text": ""}]}, "type": "video"}]}], "exercises": [{"stimuli_ids": [0], "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can talk about quality assurance.  "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can explain what quality assurance is.  "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can describe key features about quality assurance."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "How do you define an excellent program?  "}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "What do programmers do to provide the best possible version of software?"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}], "type": "group"}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have 2 tries"}, {"type": "text", "content": "you have 1 attempt left"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct", "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "try again"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time"}], "allowed_attempts": 2}}, {"type": "free_header_text", "content": "Ask your partner:"}, {"type": "free_type_text_area", "content": "Software Quality Assurance"}], "questions": [], "type": "WLC", "template_override": 1, "id": 0, "img_path": ""}, {"stimuli_ids": [1], 